    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d24-a2">

                <pb facs="0110" n="40" xml:id="pg40"/>

                <head>Earl Russell to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-02-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 26, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> With reference to my letter of the 19th
                    instant, on the subject of the steamer Oreto, which was believed from reports
                    you had received to be fitting out at Liverpool with a view to acting hostilely
                    against the people of the United States, I have the honor to transmit to you
                    herewith a copy of a letter from the commissioners of customs to the lords
                    commissioners of her Majesty’s treasury, reporting the result of the
                    investigations which they have caused to be instituted with regard to the vessel
                    in question.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUSSELL.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d24-a2-a1.xml" xpointer="d24-a2-a1"/>
            </div>
